What is a Hybrid Tractor?
Hybrid tractors are agricultural machines that integrate a diesel engine with an electric motor and battery pack, enabling power‑blending capabilities that deliver the torque of diesel while leveraging electric assistance for efficiency gains. The electric component can capture kinetic energy during braking or deceleration, store it, and redeploy it during high‑load phases, effectively extending the operational range of the diesel engine and reducing overall fuel consumption.
